    {
      "fileName": "surgical-shock.json",
      "id": "zzjfENthtRBAjqjQ",
      "name": "Surgical Shock",
      "img": "icons/sundries/books/book-red-exclamation.webp",
      "type": "feat",
      "data": {
        "_id": "zzjfENthtRBAjqjQ",
        "folder": "pb7GzzVAlrtNCQ5H",
        "img": "icons/sundries/books/book-red-exclamation.webp",
        "name": "Surgical Shock",
        "system": {
          "actionType": {
            "value": "action"
          },
          "actions": {
            "value": 1
          },
          "category": "class",
          "description": {
            "value": "<p>With a few well-placed jabs with your fist or weapon, you render your opponent disoriented or ungainly. Attempt a @Check[medicine|against:fortitude] check against the Fortitude DC of a target within your reach. The result of your check determines the severity of the condition you inflict.</p><hr /><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The target is either @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.Clumsy]{Clumsy 3} or @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.Stupefied]{Stupefied 3} until the end of your next turn. The target is then immune to Surgical Shock for 1 hour.</p>\n<p><strong>Success</strong> As critical success, but the target is either @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.Clumsy]{Clumsy 2} or @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.Stupefied]{Stupefied 2}.</p>\n<p><strong>Failure</strong> The target is minorly inconvenienced. You gain a +1 circumstance bonus to the next attack action you attempt against it before the end of your turn.</p>\n<p>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.feat-effects.Item.Effect: Surgical Shock (Failure)]</p>\n<p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The target is unaffected and you overextend yourself, triggering reactions as if you had used a manipulate action.</p>"
          },
          "level": {
            "value": 12
          },
          "prerequisites": {
            "value": [
              {
                "value": "forensic medicine methodology"
              }
            ]
          },
